###
# Multi-Tenant Messaging Platform API - Sample Requests
# Compatible with VS Code REST Client, IntelliJ HTTP Client, and cURL
###

@baseUrl = http://localhost:3000
@tenantId = tenant-a
@conversationId = conv-100

### 1. Health Check
# curl -X GET http://localhost:3000/health
GET {{baseUrl}}/health

### 2. Metrics Telemetry
# curl -X GET http://localhost:3000/metrics
GET {{baseUrl}}/metrics

### 3. Create Message (Tenant A)
# curl -X POST http://localhost:3000/api/v1/messages \
#   -H "Content-Type: application/json" \
#   -H "x-tenant-id: tenant-a" \
#   -d '{"tenantId":"tenant-a","conversationId":"conv-100","to":"+919876543210","text":"Your Order has shipped"}'
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/messages
Content-Type: application/json
x-tenant-id: {{tenantId}}

{
  "tenantId": "{{tenantId}}",
  "conversationId": "{{conversationId}}",
  "to": "+919876543210",
  "text": "Your Order has shipped"
}

### 4. Create Another Message (Tenant A)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/messages
Content-Type: application/json
x-tenant-id: {{tenantId}}

{
  "tenantId": "{{tenantId}}",
  "conversationId": "{{conversationId}}",
  "to": "+919876543210",
  "text": "Delivery expected by 2:00 PM"
}

### 5. Create Message for Tenant B (Demonstrating Multi-Tenancy)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/messages
Content-Type: application/json
x-tenant-id: tenant-b

{
  "tenantId": "tenant-b",
  "conversationId": "conv-100",
  "to": "+14155552671",
  "text": "Welcome to Tenant B workspace"
}

### 6. Get Message Details by ID (Replace :messageId with actual ID from create response)
# curl -X GET http://localhost:3000/api/v1/messages/msg-123 -H "x-tenant-id: tenant-a"
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/messages/msg-REPLACE_WITH_ID
x-tenant-id: {{tenantId}}

### 7. Provider Webhook - SENT Status Event
# curl -X POST http://localhost:3000/api/v1/webhooks/provider \
#   -H "Content-Type: application/json" \
#   -d '{"eventId":"evt-001","messageId":"msg-REPLACE_WITH_ID","status":"SENT","occurredAt":"2026-10-16T08:30:00.000Z"}'
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/webhooks/provider
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "eventId": "evt-001",
  "messageId": "msg-REPLACE_WITH_ID",
  "status": "SENT",
  "occurredAt": "2026-10-16T08:30:00.000Z"
}

### 8. Provider Webhook - DELIVERED Status Event
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/webhooks/provider
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "eventId": "evt-002",
  "messageId": "msg-REPLACE_WITH_ID",
  "status": "DELIVERED",
  "occurredAt": "2026-10-16T08:31:00.000Z"
}

### 9. Provider Webhook - Duplicate Event (Tests Idempotency - returns 200 duplicate: true)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/webhooks/provider
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "eventId": "evt-002",
  "messageId": "msg-REPLACE_WITH_ID",
  "status": "DELIVERED",
  "occurredAt": "2026-10-16T08:31:00.000Z"
}

### 10. Provider Webhook - Out-of-Order SENT event arriving after READ
# First send READ event:
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/webhooks/provider
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "eventId": "evt-003",
  "messageId": "msg-REPLACE_WITH_ID",
  "status": "READ",
  "occurredAt": "2026-10-16T08:45:00.000Z"
}

### 11. Provider Webhook - Out-of-Order SENT event arriving after READ (does not regress status!)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/webhooks/provider
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "eventId": "evt-004",
  "messageId": "msg-REPLACE_WITH_ID",
  "status": "SENT",
  "occurredAt": "2026-10-16T08:29:00.000Z"
}

### 12. Provider Webhook - Unknown Message ID (Tests 404 & Unmatched Event Strategy)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/webhooks/provider
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "eventId": "evt-unknown-999",
  "messageId": "msg-nonexistent-id",
  "status": "SENT",
  "occurredAt": "2026-10-16T08:30:00.000Z"
}

### 13. Query Conversation Messages with Pagination (Tenant A)
# curl -X GET "http://localhost:3000/api/v1/conversations/conv-100/messages?limit=20" -H "x-tenant-id: tenant-a"
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/conversations/{{conversationId}}/messages?limit=20
x-tenant-id: {{tenantId}}

### 14. Query Conversation Messages as Tenant B (Tenant Isolation - Cannot see Tenant A messages)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/conversations/{{conversationId}}/messages?limit=20
x-tenant-id: tenant-b

### 15. Validation Failure - Invalid Phone & Missing Text (Returns 400 Bad Request)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/messages
Content-Type: application/json
x-tenant-id: {{tenantId}}

{
  "tenantId": "tenant-a",
  "conversationId": "conv-100",
  "to": "123-bad-phone",
  "text": ""
}
